    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Mistral Ministral is a small, cheap, open weights line. All 3 versions publish open weights, and none support reasoning. Context windows run from 131072 to 262144 tokens across the family, with the newest versions reaching the top of that range. Output limits are large, up to 209715 tokens on the 8B and 14B versions. Input can include images alongside text, and output is text only. Pricing is low, from $0.1 to $0.2 per million input and output tokens. The spread of versions, 3B, 8B and 14B, lets you trade cost against capability. This suits high volume work, long document or image reading, and self hosting where open weights matter. The limits are the absence of reasoning support and the small model sizes, so hard multi step problems and tasks needing strong reasoning are a poor fit.",
